      "content": "This critique is absolutely seen as a legitimate and central historical argument, not just as cynicism. Scholars often discuss the \"realist\" perspective, which posits that great power politics, like the power dynamics within the UN Security Council, ultimately dictate the organization's actions. While some see the critique as anti-globalist, the analysis of power imbalances is a core, evidence-based part of contemporary international relations theory.",
